@call c04 diabetic_dextrose start=07:22:45
@patient age=54 sex=female weight_kg=82 complaint="confused and sweaty, not acting right" allergies=sulfa home_meds="insulin, metformin" history="type 1 diabetes"
@traps hypoglycemia
RD: Medic 21, altered mental status, fifty-four year old female, known diabetic.  >> dispatch:altered mental status "altered mental status"
GAP 3
M1: Medic 21 on scene.  >> time:eTimes.06 "on scene"
GAP 3
BY: She took her insulin this morning but she didn't eat. Now she's not making sense.
M1: Ma'am, can you tell me your name? She's confused, pale, cool and diaphoretic.  >> status:pale, cool and diaphoretic "pale, cool and diaphoretic"
TAP knock +label
M2: BGL 42.  >> vital:bgl=42 "BGL 42"
M1: Okay, can she swallow? No, she's too altered. Get me a line.
GAP 6
TAP snap +label
M2: Twenty gauge, left forearm.  >> proc:IV access "Twenty gauge, left forearm"
GAP 3
TAP button +label
M1: D10, 100 mLs IV.  >> med:dextrose,100,mL,IV "D10, 100 mLs IV"
GAP 12
TAP button -
GAP 12
M2: Vitals, BP 134 over 78, heart rate 96, resps 18.  >> vital:bp=134/78 "BP 134 over 78"; vital:hr=96 "heart rate 96"; vital:rr=18 "resps 18"
GAP 8
M2: Recheck sugar is 68.  >> vital:bgl=68 "sugar is 68"
GAP 2
TAP knock +label
M1: Hang another 100 of D10.  >> med:dextrose,100,, "another 100 of D10"
GAP 10
PT: Oh. Oh no. Did I go low again?
M1: You did. Sugar's coming up. Any allergies?
PT: Sulfa.
M2: Sugar's 124 now, she's A and O times four.  >> vital:bgl=124 "Sugar's 124"; status:A&O×4 "A and O times four"
GAP 5
PT: I don't want to go to the hospital, I feel fine now.
M1: Your sugar was really low. With the insulin, it could drop again. We'd like to take you in.
PT: Okay. Okay, fine.
M1: Transporting to University.  >> time:eTimes.09 "Transporting"
